<title>CANADA: Pierre Fabre to distribute Biovail drug.</title>
<headline>Pierre Fabre to distribute Biovail drug.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biovail Corp International said on Monday that it appointed French privately held Pierre Fabre S.A. as marketing partner to distribute its hypertension drug Tiazac in France.</p>
<p>France is Europe's largest market for this type of drug, called diltiazem, with annual sales of C$120 million, the Toronto-based pharmaceutical firm said.</p>
<p>&quot;We anticipate that product launches will begin in the second half of 1997,&quot; said Biovail's chairman Eugene Melnyk.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
